    "Pass a live theme token as `color` and the sample follows the active scheme; a hairline edge keeps a white or near-black sample visible on the surface behind it. The value lines are set in mono, and the lockup comes in two more sizes (`small`, `large`), as a `circle`, `inline` (the label beside the block), or as a `block` (a full-width ramp bar).",
    "A palette picker takes one of the kit's five accent palettes, `violet`, `cyan`, `mint`, `rose` or `amber` (ThemeProvider's precedence: cyan, mint, rose, amber, violet), with `selected` and `onPress`. It is a 16px disc of the palette's hue, the same in both schemes, and a radio named for its palette (\"Violet\"). The palette in force wears the selection ring, a 2px gap in the card color and then a 2px muted-foreground band; the others draw none. On the web a hovered disc grows to 1.25 times its size. Put the pickers in a `radiogroup` so the set reads as one choice. A plain sample still uses `color`.",
